<section class="feat f-pur" id="cli" aria-labelledby="h-cli">
 <div class="wrap">
  <div class="fh">
   <div>
    <p class="tag"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#g-tag"/></svg>03 · tnctl + MCP</p>
    <h2 id="h-cli">The whole fleet in your terminal. And in your coding agent.</h2>
    <p class="lede"><code>tnctl</code> scripts everything the console does. <code>tnctl agent install</code> gives Claude Code, Codex or any agent the fleet through MCP: reads within your rights, changes through tnctl.</p>
   </div>
   <ul class="caps">
    <li><h3>One binary, one login</h3><p>macOS, Linux, Windows. Robots, config, bots, logs, live MQTT.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Safe changes</h3><p><code>--dry-run</code>, then <code>--wait=ready</code> until every robot confirms.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Ansible inventory</h3><p>Playbooks on the live fleet; SSH, port-forward, SOCKS.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Laptop to bot</h3><p>A script you write on your laptop runs unchanged on a TeknoirBot, 24/7.</p></li>
   </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="vis">
  <div class="duo">
   <figure class="frame term" role="img" aria-label="A terminal session at 08:30: tnctl lists three arms with gripper drift on firmware 3.8, streams their live MQTT, pins firmware 3.7 on arm-11 with a dry run, waits until it is ready and the gripper has re-homed to zero drift, and opens SSH on arm-11">
    <div class="wbar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>maria@laptop: ~/pickers</span></div>
<pre><span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">tnctl robots fleet=pickers-eu --problems</span>
<span class="h">NAME     <span class="xm">TYPE     </span>FIRMWARE  PROBLEM</span>
arm-07   <span class="xm">ur-cell  </span>3.8       <span class="w">gripper drift +4.1 mm</span>
arm-11   <span class="xm">ur-cell  </span>3.8       <span class="w">gripper drift +4.1 mm</span>
arm-19   <span class="xm">ur-cell  </span>3.8       <span class="w">gripper drift +3.9 mm</span>
<span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">tnctl mqtt sub 'robots/arm-11/gripper/#'</span>
<span class="o">gripper/state</span>  drift_mm=4.12  force_n=38.7
<span class="o">gripper/state</span>  drift_mm=4.14  force_n=38.9
<span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">tnctl config override arm-11 \</span>
<span class="c">    gripper.firmware=3.7 --dry-run</span>
<span class="y">~ gripper.firmware</span>   3.8 → 3.7<span class="xm">   <span class="o">layer override</span></span>
<span class="o">1 robot · 1 change · nothing sent</span>
<span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">tnctl config override arm-11 \</span>
<span class="c">    gripper.firmware=3.7 --wait=ready</span>
published <span class="k">1/1 ✓</span>  applied <span class="k">1/1 ✓</span>  ready <span class="k">1/1 ✓</span><span class="xm">  <span class="o">38 s</span></span>
<span class="o">gripper re-homed</span>  drift_mm=<span class="k">0.00</span>
<span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">tnctl ssh arm-11</span>
<span class="o">maria@arm-11:~$</span> <span class="cur"></span></pre>
   </figure>
   <figure class="frame agent" role="img" aria-label="A coding agent using the Teknoir MCP server: it reads problems, PromQL, live MQTT and config, confirms the bot's finding F-212, proposes pinning firmware 3.7 on arm-11 first with a tnctl dry run, and applies it with tnctl after Maria approves">
    <div class="wbar"><span class="w0">Coding agent · ~/pickers</span><span class="st">reads as maria · writes via tnctl</span><span class="mcp"><i class="dot g"></i>MCP · teknoir</span></div>
    <div class="ag">
     <div class="you">Why are three arms in pickers-eu dropping grasps?</div>
     <div class="tc"><i></i><b>teknoir.list_problems</b><span>fleet=pickers-eu</span><em>F-212 +2</em></div>
     <div class="tc"><i></i><b>teknoir.promql</b><span>rate(grasp_fail_total[6d]) by robot</span><em>3 series</em></div>
     <div class="tc"><i></i><b>teknoir.mqtt_sample</b><span>robots/arm-11/gripper</span><em>20 msgs</em></div>
     <div class="tc"><i></i><b>teknoir.config_get</b><span>robot/arm-11 gripper</span><em>firmware 3.8</em></div>
     <div class="say">The bot's finding <b>F-212</b> holds: only <b class="nw">arm-07, arm-11</b> and <b class="nw">arm-19</b> run gripper firmware 3.8; their zero point drifts about 0.7 mm a day since the update. Pin 3.7 on those three, <span class="nw">arm-11</span> first. Dry run:</div>
     <div class="tc tn"><i></i><b>tnctl config override <span class="nw">--dry-run</span></b><span>arm-11 gripper.firmware=3.7</span><em>1 robot</em></div>
     <div class="ask">Apply to arm-11 and wait for ready? <s>Show diff</s><b>Apply with tnctl</b></div>
     <div class="tc tn"><i></i><b>tnctl config override <span class="nw">--wait=ready</span></b><span>arm-11</span><em>ready 1/1</em></div>
     <div class="prompt">Ask about your fleet…</div>
    </div>
   </figure>
  </div>
  </div>
